<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP SCORES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP SCORES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results and close of play scores</p>
<p>on the third day of four-day English County Championship cricket</p>
<p>matches on Friday:</p>
<p>At Edgbaston: Warwickshire beat Yorkshire by four wickets.</p>
<p>Yorkshire 233 and 154. Warwickshire 140 and 249-6 (D.Brown 65</p>
<p>not out; D.Gough 4-65). Warwickshire 20 points Yorkshire 5.</p>
<p>At The Oval: Gloucestershire beat Surrey by nine wickets.</p>
<p>Surrey 115 and 269 (G.Thorpe 81; M.Alleyne 6-64).</p>
<p>Gloucestershire 371 and 15-1. Gloucester 24 points Surrey 4.</p>
<p>At Lord's: Middlesex beat Derbyshire by 131 runs. Middlesex</p>
<p>146 and 262 (K.Brown 76, J.Kallis 52; D.Malcolm 6-75).</p>
<p>Derbyshire 178 and 99 (R.Johnson 4-26). Middlesex 20 points</p>
<p>Derbyshire 4.</p>
<p>At Chelmsford: Essex 237 and 309-5 (S.Law 81 not out,</p>
<p>P.Prichard 80, N7). Durham 291 (M.Speight 53).</p>
<p>At Southampton: Hampshire 285 and 182 (A.Pierson 4-58).</p>
<p>Leicestershire 349 (D.Millns 114 not out) and 31-0.</p>
<p>At Canterbury: Glamorgan 279 and 193 (S.James 54; P.Strang</p>
<p>4-59, M.Fleming 4-28).Kent 154 and 156-3 (A.Wells 84 not out).</p>
<p>At Old Trafford: Lancashire 125 and 357 (J.Crawley 101,</p>
<p>M.Atherton 68, G.Lloyd 62). Nottinghamshire 263 and 30-0.</p>
<p>At Taunton: Sussex 241 and 142-3 (C.Athey 70 not out).</p>
<p>Somerset 409.</p>
<p>Other results:</p>
<p>At Fenner's: Cambridge University v Northamptonshire match</p>
<p>drawn. Cambridge University 280-9 declared and 61-3.</p>
<p>Northamptonshire 367-8 declared (R.Bailey 105, A.Penberthy 56).</p>
<p>At The Parks: Oxford University v Worcestershire match</p>
<p>drawn. Worcestershire 359-2 declared and 192-6 declared</p>
<p>(V.Solanki 128 not out). Oxford University 281-8 declared and</p>
<p>135-7.</p>
